From 9c5bdfc21fbc4de6de1d262cfd0251111a5cba40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:17:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0432-starbite-m11b-ncm.patch - StarbiteUSBNCM built in
 for STARLTE (copy of starbite/apple-drivers/StarbiteUSB/StarbiteUSBNCM.* at
 0d957fd, STARLTE-only build unit with __PRIVATE_SPI__ like the family, so
 IONetworkController's vtable slots 2-5 resolve) as an IOEthernetController on
 StarbiteUSB (sbusb=1); sbstop=ncm, the M11b test without user space:
 StarbiteM11b.cpp waits for its IOEthernetInterface, names it through
 IONetworkStack (as IORegisterNetworkInterface does for a network root),
 bsd/dev/starlte_m11b.c brings it up, attaches IPv6 and starts the EUI-64
 link-local address through ifioctl() on kernel sockets (SIOCSIFFLAGS,
 SIOCPROTOATTACH_IN6, SIOCLL_START, as configd would), then XNU's ICMPv6
 counters: each echo reply the stack sends is an "M11b PASS" line, and after
 the third (plus the Mac's last pings or 3 s) the boot stops into TWRP

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
